\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 1. USER-PROVIDED LOCATION OVERRIDES VISUAL GUESSING\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b0\fs24 \cf0 In normal use, the user may provide the location or attraction name together with the photograph.\
When this happens:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 USE THE USER-PROVIDED LOCATION DIRECTLY.
\f3\b0 \
Do not independently replace it with a more famous or visually similar place.\
User-provided information should control:\
the main location typography,\uc0\u8232 English archival caption,\u8232 bottom information panel,\u8232 postmark wording,\u8232 and geographic metadata.\
Do not silently upgrade the place to a more specific location than the user supplied.\
If the user supplies only:\

\f0\b NINGBO
