\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 5. ANTI-CIRCULAR IDENTIFICATION RULE\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f3\b0\fs24 \cf0 A candidate generated by the model cannot later become evidence supporting itself.\
Forbidden reasoning:\
\'93This looks like West Lake.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f4 \cf0 \uc0\u8594 
\f3  therefore Hangzhou is likely.\

\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f3  therefore this architecture probably belongs to West Lake.\

\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f3  therefore West Lake is verified.\
This is circular reasoning.\
It is prohibited.\
The same applies to:\
Kyoto,\uc0\u8232 Suzhou,\u8232 Beijing,\u8232 Shanghai,\u8232 Paris,\u8232 Venice,\u8232 or any famous destination.\
Candidate generation and verification must remain separate.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
